IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `limitation-core`

-- Limitation of Actions Act 1958 (Vic) -- the seat of the injured person (or, after a death, the estate or the
-- dependants) asking whether, and until when, they can still sue. Each question is asked as that person would ask
-- it, with plain inputs; the rules are in limitation-core.l4 and none is restated here. Judgments the Act leaves to a
-- court (ought to have known, just and reasonable, close associate) are asked as facts or as "would a court find".
-- BASELINE, not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Limitation of Actions Act 1958 (Vic) -- questions for the person who wants to sue`

§§ `Which time limit applies`

@export Which time limit of the Limitation of Actions Act 1958 (Vic) applies to my claim: none (dust disease of a worker, child abuse), the personal injury rules of Part IIA, the old law kept for workplace and transport accident claims, or the 3- or 6-year periods of Part I? Answers nothing for a kind of action this encoding does not cover.
GIVEN `my claim is` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc What kind of claim is it: damages for my own personal injury; a survivor action by the estate of a person who died; a dependants' action for a death under Wrongs Act 1958 Part III; contract or tort not for death or personal injury and not defamation; or another kind of action
      `my claim comes under` IS A `Compensation scheme` @desc Is the action for damages one to which the Accident Compensation Act 1985 Part IV or the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 Part 7 applies, one for an injury that entitles a worker to compensation under the Workers Compensation Act 1958, one to which the Transport Accident Act 1986 Part 6 or Part 10 applies, or none of these?
      `the injury is a dust-related condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the injury a dust-related condition within the meaning of the Administration and Probate Act 1958 (for example asbestosis, mesothelioma or silicosis)?
      `the injured person was a worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the injured person a worker who got the injury as a worker?
      `the action comes under the workplace or Wrongs Act damages Parts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an action to which the Accident Compensation Act 1985 Part IV, the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 Part 7, or Part III or Part VB of the Wrongs Act 1958 applies? (Wrongs Act Part VB applies to most claims for personal injury damages caused by fault.)
      `the injury results from tobacco` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the injury result from smoking or other use of tobacco products, or exposure to tobacco smoke?
      `the injury results from abuse as a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the death or injury result from physical or sexual abuse of the person when they were under 18 (with any psychological abuse arising from it)?
      `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE @desc The day of the act or omission said to have caused the death or injury (ISO date, e.g. 2024-03-15); for contract or tort, the day the cause of action arose
GIVETH A MAYBE `Limitation regime`
`Which time limit applies to my claim` `my claim is` `my claim comes under` `the injury is a dust-related condition` `the injured person was a worker` `the action comes under the workplace or Wrongs Act damages Parts` `the injury results from tobacco` `the injury results from abuse as a child` `the day of the act or omission` MEANS
    `the limitation regime` `my claim is` `my claim comes under` `the injury is a dust-related condition` `the injured person was a worker` `the action comes under the workplace or Wrongs Act damages Parts` `the injury results from tobacco` `the injury results from abuse as a child` `the day of the act or omission`

@export Does Part IIA of the Limitation of Actions Act 1958 (Vic) -- the time limits for personal injury and death claims -- apply to my claim (s 27B)? Answers nothing if the claim is not for death or personal injury.
GIVEN `my claim is` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc What kind of claim is it: damages for my own personal injury; a survivor action by the estate; a dependants' action for a death under Wrongs Act 1958 Part III; contract or tort not for death or personal injury; or another kind of action
      `my claim comes under` IS A `Compensation scheme` @desc Does a workplace or transport accident scheme apply to the action (Accident Compensation Act 1985 Part IV or WIRC Act 2013 Part 7; Workers Compensation Act 1958; Transport Accident Act 1986 Part 6 or 10), or none?
      `the injury is a dust-related condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the injury a dust-related condition within the meaning of the Administration and Probate Act 1958?
      `the injury results from tobacco` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the injury result from smoking or other use of tobacco products, or exposure to tobacco smoke?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does Part IIA apply to my claim` `my claim is` `my claim comes under` `the injury is a dust-related condition` `the injury results from tobacco` MEANS
    `s 27B -- Part IIA applies` `my claim is` `my claim comes under` `the injury is a dust-related condition` `the injury results from tobacco`

§§ `When my claim became discoverable (Part IIA)`

@export On what day did my cause of action become discoverable (s 27F)? The first day I knew, or ought to have known by taking all reasonable steps, that the death or injury happened, that it was caused by the defendant's fault, and (for an injury) that it was serious enough to justify suing; for a dependants' claim for a death, not before the death.
GIVEN `the day I knew of the death or injury` IS A DATE @desc The first day you knew, or would have found out had you taken all reasonable steps, that the death or injury had occurred (ISO date). For a minor or incapacitated person not under a legal incapacity, what a capable parent or guardian knew counts (s 27J(3)).
      `the day I knew it was the defendant's fault` IS A DATE @desc The first day you knew, or would have found out by taking all reasonable steps, that it was caused by the fault of the defendant (ISO date)
      `the day I knew the injury was serious enough to sue` IS A DATE @desc For an injury: the first day you knew, or ought to have known, that it was serious enough to justify bringing an action (ISO date; for a death claim, any date)
      `my claim is for a death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim founded on a death rather than an injury?
      `my claim is a dependants' claim for a death under Wrongs Act Part III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an action by the dependants for a wrongful death under Part III of the Wrongs Act 1958?
      `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc For a death claim, the day of death (ISO date; otherwise any date)
GIVETH A DATE
`On what day did my claim become discoverable` `the day I knew of the death or injury` `the day I knew it was the defendant's fault` `the day I knew the injury was serious enough to sue` `my claim is for a death` `my claim is a dependants' claim for a death under Wrongs Act Part III` `the day of death` MEANS
    `s 27F -- the day the cause of action is discoverable` `the day I knew of the death or injury` `the day I knew it was the defendant's fault` `the day I knew the injury was serious enough to sue` `my claim is for a death` `my claim is a dependants' claim for a death under Wrongs Act Part III` `the day of death`

§§ `The last day to sue for my own injury (Part IIA)`

@export What is the last day I can start my action for my own personal injury under Part IIA (ss 27D, 27E, 27I, 27J)? The earlier of 3 years from discoverability (6 if I was a minor or of unsound mind at the time) and 12 years from the act or omission, with special rules for a child injured by a parent, guardian or close associate, and time added while I was under a legal incapacity. Answers nothing for an act before 21 May 2003, where the earlier law may cut it short (s 27N(4)).
GIVEN `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE @desc The day of the act or omission said to have caused the injury (ISO date)
      `the day my claim became discoverable` IS A DATE @desc The day your cause of action became discoverable (see the question on discoverability, s 27F; ISO date)
      `my birthday` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (ISO date)
      `I was of unsound mind at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the act or omission, were you of unsound mind, or a represented person under the Guardianship and Administration Act 2019?
      `the defendant was my parent or guardian or their close associate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were under 18 at the time: was the person you are suing then your parent or guardian, or someone so close to your parent or guardian that the parent might be influenced not to sue them for you, or that you might be unwilling to tell your parent or guardian what happened?
      `my legal incapacity` IS A `Kind of legal incapacity` @desc Since the time limit began to run, have you been under a legal incapacity: a minor not in the custody of a parent or guardian able to act; or a person unable (or substantially impeded) to manage your affairs about this claim because of a disease or impairment, for 28 days or more in a row, without a guardian or administrator authorised to sue for you; or neither?
      `my incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day that legal incapacity began (ISO date; otherwise any date)
      `my incapacity ended` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it ended, or the day you expect it to end (ISO date; otherwise any date)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`What is the last day I can sue for my injury` `the day of the act or omission` `the day my claim became discoverable` `my birthday` `I was of unsound mind at the time` `the defendant was my parent or guardian or their close associate` `my legal incapacity` `my incapacity began` `my incapacity ended` MEANS
    `ss 27D, 27E, 27I, 27J -- the last day for the injured person's action` `the day of the act or omission` `the day my claim became discoverable` `my birthday` `I was of unsound mind at the time` `the defendant was my parent or guardian or their close associate` `my legal incapacity` `my incapacity began` `my incapacity ended`

§§ `The last day to sue after a death (Part IIA)`
-- Situation: the injured person has died, and you are their executor or administrator, or one of their dependants.

@export As executor or administrator, what is the last day the estate can bring the deceased's own claim for their injury (a survivor action, ss 27D, 27E, 27G, 27I)? Answers nothing for an act before 21 May 2003 (s 27N(4)).
GIVEN `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE @desc The day of the act or omission said to have caused the deceased's injury (ISO date)
      `the deceased's birthday` IS A DATE @desc The deceased's date of birth (ISO date)
      `the deceased was of unsound mind at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the act or omission, was the deceased of unsound mind, or a represented person?
      `the defendant was the deceased's parent or guardian or their close associate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the deceased was under 18 at the time: was the defendant then their parent or guardian, or a close associate of one?
      `the deceased could discover the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the claim become discoverable by the deceased before they died?
      `the day it was discoverable by the deceased` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it became discoverable by the deceased (ISO date; otherwise any date)
      `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc The day the deceased died (ISO date)
      `the day of my appointment` IS A DATE @desc The day you were appointed executor or administrator (ISO date)
      `the day it was discoverable by me` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim became discoverable by you (s 27F; ISO date)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`What is the last day the estate can sue for the deceased's injury` `the day of the act or omission` `the deceased's birthday` `the deceased was of unsound mind at the time` `the defendant was the deceased's parent or guardian or their close associate` `the deceased could discover the claim` `the day it was discoverable by the deceased` `the day of death` `the day of my appointment` `the day it was discoverable by me` MEANS
    `ss 27D, 27E, 27G, 27I -- the last day for a survivor action` `the day of the act or omission` `the deceased's birthday` `the deceased was of unsound mind at the time` `the defendant was the deceased's parent or guardian or their close associate` `the deceased could discover the claim` `the day it was discoverable by the deceased` `the day of death` `the day of my appointment` `the day it was discoverable by me`

@export As a dependant, what is the last day to sue for the death under Part III of the Wrongs Act 1958 (ss 27D, 27F(4), 27H, 27Q)? 3 years from discoverability (never before the death) or 12 years from the death, whichever ends first; for a death from child abuse, 3 years with no long-stop. Answers nothing for an act before 21 May 2003, or a child killed by a parent, guardian or close associate, where the Act is unclear.
GIVEN `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE @desc The day of the act or omission said to have caused the death (ISO date)
      `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc The day of death (ISO date)
      `the day the claim was discoverable` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim became discoverable by you (s 27F; ISO date)
      `the death resulted from abuse as a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the death result from physical or sexual abuse of the deceased when they were under 18?
      `the deceased was a child killed by a parent or guardian or their close associate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the deceased under 18 at the act or omission, and the defendant then their parent or guardian or a close associate of one?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`What is the last day dependants can sue for the death` `the day of the act or omission` `the day of death` `the day the claim was discoverable` `the death resulted from abuse as a child` `the deceased was a child killed by a parent or guardian or their close associate` MEANS
    `ss 27D, 27F(4), 27H, 27Q -- the last day for a dependants' action for a death` `the day of the act or omission` `the day of death` `the day the claim was discoverable` `the death resulted from abuse as a child` `the deceased was a child killed by a parent or guardian or their close associate`

§§ `Asking the court for more time`
-- Situation: your time limit has run out, or is about to.

@export Can I apply to a court to extend my time limit (ss 27K, 27M, 27O, 23A)? Yes under Part IIA (even after it expired or after I have started an action) and for other personal injury negligence claims; no for a child abuse claim, which has no time limit. Answers nothing where the Act gives no power.
GIVEN `the time limit that applies` IS A `Limitation regime` @desc The time limit that applies to your claim, as answered by the question "Which time limit applies to my claim"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I apply to a court to extend my time limit` `the time limit that applies` MEANS
    `ss 27K, 27M, 23A -- I may apply to a court to extend the period` `the time limit that applies`

@export If the court extends my time limit, what is my new last day (s 27K(3))? The court decides whether an extension is just and reasonable, and for how long, having regard to the s 27L matters; the extension holds for an action in that court.
GIVEN `my last day without an extension` IS A DATE @desc Your last day to sue as the Act sets it (ISO date)
      `the court orders an extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court decided it is just and reasonable to extend the period? It looks at all the circumstances, including the length of and reasons for the delay, prejudice to the defendant (including to a fair trial), what the defendant did to let you find out the facts, any disability or legal incapacity after discoverability, how long the claim took to become discoverable, whether you acted promptly once you knew you might have a claim, the advice you sought and got, the nature and extent of your loss, and the nature of the defendant's conduct (s 27L).
      `days of extension` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days the court extended the period by
GIVETH A DATE
`What is my last day after an extension by the court` `my last day without an extension` `the court orders an extension` `days of extension` MEANS
    `s 27K(3) -- the last day after an extension` `my last day without an extension` `the court orders an extension` `days of extension`

§§ `Child abuse claims: earlier judgments and settlements (Part IIA Division 5)`
-- Situation: you were abused as a child, and an earlier claim was dismissed, decided or settled.

@export I was abused as a child and my earlier claim was dismissed as out of time, decided, or settled. Can I bring an action on it again (s 27QA)? Answers no if a National Redress Scheme release or accepted offer covers it; nothing where s 27QA does not reach the earlier outcome.
GIVEN `the earlier outcome` IS AN `Earlier outcome` @desc What happened to the earlier claim: no earlier judgment or settlement; dismissed as out of time, or an extension refused; another judgment or order, including a dismissal; or settled by a settlement agreement
      `the day of the earlier outcome` IS A DATE @desc The day of that judgment, order or settlement (ISO date)
      `my time limit had expired before 1 July 2015` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had any time limit that applied to the claim expired before 1 July 2015?
      `a National Redress Scheme release covers it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a deed of release or accepted offer of redress under the National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) for it, or was the settlement taken into account in one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I sue again on my child abuse claim` `the earlier outcome` `the day of the earlier outcome` `my time limit had expired before 1 July 2015` `a National Redress Scheme release covers it` MEANS
    `s 27QA -- an action may be brought despite the earlier outcome` `the earlier outcome` `the day of the earlier outcome` `my time limit had expired before 1 July 2015` `a National Redress Scheme release covers it`

@export Can the court hearing my new child abuse claim set aside the earlier judgment, order or settlement (ss 27QB-27QE, 27R)? Only the Supreme Court may set aside another court's judgment, order or settlement (but not the High Court's), and only if it is just and reasonable.
GIVEN `a court gave effect to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the earlier judgment, order or settlement made by, or given effect by an order of, a court?
      `it was the court now hearing my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is that the same court that is hearing your new claim?
      `it was the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, was it the High Court of Australia?
      `my claim is in the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your new claim in the Supreme Court of Victoria?
      `the court finds it just and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the court be satisfied that it is just and reasonable to set it aside?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the court set aside my earlier judgment or settlement` `a court gave effect to it` `it was the court now hearing my claim` `it was the High Court` `my claim is in the Supreme Court` `the court finds it just and reasonable` MEANS
        `ss 27QB, 27QD, 27R -- the court hearing the action has power to set it aside` `a court gave effect to it` `it was the court now hearing my claim` `it was the High Court` `my claim is in the Supreme Court`
    AND `the court finds it just and reasonable`

@export If my earlier child abuse judgment or settlement is set aside, can whoever paid me under it get the money back because it was set aside (s 27QF)? No. Answers nothing if nothing has been set aside.
GIVEN `it has been set aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court set aside the earlier judgment or settlement agreement (wholly or in part)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the payer recover what it paid me` `it has been set aside` MEANS
    `s 27QF -- the payer may recover what it paid` `it has been set aside`

@export In my new child abuse claim, can the court take into account what I was paid under the judgment or settlement that was set aside, when awarding damages and costs (ss 27QC(2), 27QE(2))?
GIVEN `it has been set aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the earlier judgment or settlement been set aside?
      `the court finds it just and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the court be satisfied it is just and reasonable to take those amounts into account?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the court take into account what I was paid before` `it has been set aside` `the court finds it just and reasonable` MEANS
    `ss 27QC(2), 27QE(2) -- earlier payments may be taken into account` `it has been set aside` `the court finds it just and reasonable`

@export Do the 2026 changes to the child abuse rules (Justice Legislation Amendment (Vicarious Liability for Child Abuse) Act 2026) apply to my claim (s 27T)? Yes if, between 13 November 2024 and 25 February 2026, it was settled, determined by a court, or started and not yet settled or determined. Answers nothing otherwise.
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened in the window` @desc What happened to the claim between 13 November 2024 and 25 February 2026: it was settled; it was determined by a court, including by dismissal; it was commenced and was still open on 25 February 2026; or none of these
      `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day it was settled, determined or commenced (ISO date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do the 2026 changes apply to my child abuse claim` `what happened` `the day it happened` MEANS
    `s 27T -- the 2026 amendments reach the cause of action` `what happened` `the day it happened`

§§ `The last day to sue outside Part IIA (Part I and Part II)`
-- Situation: your claim is not under Part IIA (for example a contract or tort claim, or a tobacco claim).

@export What is the last day I can sue on a claim outside Part IIA (ss 5, 23, 27)? 6 years from when the cause of action accrued for contract or tort, 3 years for personal injury (for a disease, from when I first knew of it and that someone caused it); later if fraud or mistake hid it, or if I was a minor or of unsound mind when it accrued.
GIVEN `my action is for` IS A `Part I action` @desc What the action is for: contract or tort, other than personal injury; personal injury; or personal injury that is a disease or disorder
      `the day my cause of action accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day the cause of action accrued (for most contract and tort claims, the breach or the day damage was suffered; ISO date)
      `the day I first knew of the disease and its cause` IS A DATE @desc For a disease or disorder: the day you first knew you had it and that it was caused by someone's act or omission (ISO date; otherwise any date)
      `fraud or mistake hid my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action based on the defendant's fraud, was it concealed by fraud, or is it for relief from a mistake?
      `the day I discovered it` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you discovered the fraud or mistake, or could have with reasonable diligence (ISO date; otherwise any date)
      `I was under a disability when it accrued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When the cause of action accrued, were you under 18 or of unsound mind?
      `the day my disability ended` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you turned 18 or stopped being of unsound mind, or died, whichever came first (ISO date; otherwise any date)
      `I claim through someone who was not under a disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the right first accrue to someone not under a disability, through whom you claim?
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day I can sue outside Part IIA` `my action is for` `the day my cause of action accrued` `the day I first knew of the disease and its cause` `fraud or mistake hid my claim` `the day I discovered it` `I was under a disability when it accrued` `the day my disability ended` `I claim through someone who was not under a disability` MEANS
    `ss 5, 23, 27 -- the last day for a Part I action` `my action is for` `the day my cause of action accrued` `the day I first knew of the disease and its cause` `fraud or mistake hid my claim` `the day I discovered it` `I was under a disability when it accrued` `the day my disability ended` `I claim through someone who was not under a disability`

§§ `Am I in time`

@export If I start my action on a given day, am I in time? Yes if that day is on or before my last day.
GIVEN `the day I start my action` IS A DATE @desc The day the action is (or will be) commenced (ISO date)
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc Your last day to sue, from one of the questions above (ISO date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I in time if I start my action on this day` `the day I start my action` `my last day` MEANS
    `the action is in time` `the day I start my action` `my last day`
